---
// one-receptor-many-outlets — the central idea of the MC5R page. The same
// melanocortin signal (α-MSH / ACTH) reaching MC5R fans out to three kinds of
// peripheral work: the body's surface glands (sebum, tears, Harderian
// porphyrins), fuel handling in muscle and fat, and a regulatory arm of the
// immune system. Schematic; SVG-only, wrap in <Figure>.
---

<svg
  class="orm-fig"
  viewBox="0 0 640 320"
  role="img"
  aria-labelledby="orm-t orm-d"
  xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
>
  <title id="orm-t">One receptor, many outlets: what MC5R does in the periphery</title>
  <desc id="orm-d"
    >Alpha-MSH and ACTH act on MC5R, which fans out to three kinds of work at
    the body's periphery. Surface glands: sebum that waterproofs skin and fur,
    tear-gland protein, and Harderian-gland porphyrins. Fuel: fatty-acid
    oxidation and glucose uptake in skeletal muscle, and lipolysis in fat
    cells. Immunity: the melanocortin-driven regulatory cells that calm
    autoimmune inflammation.</desc
  >

  <!-- source: the signal -->
  <rect class="card src" x="20" y="40" width="150" height="62" rx="12" />
  <text x="95" y="66" text-anchor="middle" class="card-t">α-MSH · ACTH</text>
  <text x="95" y="84" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">the melanocortin signal</text>

  <!-- hub: MC5R -->
  <rect class="card hot" x="20" y="150" width="150" height="70" rx="12" />
  <text x="95" y="180" text-anchor="middle" class="rec hot-t">MC5R</text>
  <text x="95" y="198" text-anchor="middle" class="sub">Gs → cAMP</text>

  <!-- signal → hub -->
  <path class="branch hot" d="M95 102 L95 150" />
  <polygon class="arrow" points="90,142 100,142 95,150" />

  <!-- branches hub → outlets -->
  <path class="branch hot" d="M170 185 C 260 185, 260 64, 350 64" />
  <path class="branch" d="M170 185 C 260 185, 260 174, 350 174" />
  <path class="branch" d="M170 185 C 260 185, 260 272, 350 272" />

  <!-- travelling emphasis dot toward the glands -->
  <circle class="pulse" r="4">
    <animateMotion dur="3.4s" repeatCount="indefinite" keyPoints="0;1" keyTimes="0;1"
      path="M170 185 C 260 185, 260 64, 350 64" />
  </circle>

  <!-- outlet 1: surface glands -->
  <rect class="card hot" x="352" y="22" width="268" height="84" rx="12" />
  <text x="368" y="46" class="head hot-t">Surface glands</text>
  <text x="368" y="64" class="line">sebum — waterproofing skin &amp; fur</text>
  <text x="368" y="80" class="line">lacrimal protein · Harderian porphyrins</text>
  <text x="368" y="96" class="tag">the signature role</text>

  <!-- outlet 2: fuel -->
  <rect class="card" x="352" y="132" width="268" height="84" rx="12" />
  <text x="368" y="156" class="head">Fuel handling</text>
  <text x="368" y="174" class="line">muscle — fat oxidation, glucose uptake</text>
  <text x="368" y="190" class="line">fat cells — lipolysis</text>
  <text x="368" y="206" class="tag">emerging</text>

  <!-- outlet 3: immunity -->
  <rect class="card" x="352" y="242" width="268" height="66" rx="12" />
  <text x="368" y="266" class="head">Regulatory immunity</text>
  <text x="368" y="284" class="line">Treg-inducing cells in the spleen</text>
  <text x="368" y="300" class="tag">post-autoimmune recovery</text>
</svg>

